### 3. Git Commands to Push to GitHub

```bash
cd /app/my_website

# Add the remote (replace URL with your actual repo URL)
git remote add origin https://github.com/lydia-moreno/my_website.git

# Push the main branch
git push -u origin main

# Create the gh-pages branch for GitHub Pages deployment
git push origin main:gh-pages

# Trigger the workflow manually (or push to main to auto-trigger)
# The workflow will run automatically on push to main
```

To **run existing GitHub workflows** (the deploy workflow), push to `main` as shown above, or use the GitHub CLI:
```bash
gh workflow run deploy.yml --ref main
